            <ArticleTitle>Thoracoscopic renal denervation for intractable autosomal dominant polycystic kidney disease-related pain.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>161-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The authors report a case of intractable autosomal dominant polycystic kidney disease-related pain associated with normal renal function, treated with renal denervation. Renal denervation was performed via a thoracoscopic approach. The good medium-term result suggests that thoracoscopic sympatho-splanchnicectomy would be an attractive procedure for pain management in autosomal polycystic kidney disease.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
